1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,560
Hey, Mr. Hitoma.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:05,210
What is it, Haneda?

3
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:09,050
Is it okay to have just one 
graduation ceremony for Isaki?

4
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:12,380
Most people only ever get one.

5
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:14,030
We heard about it from Isaki.

6
00:00:14,470 --> 00:00:17,900
Once she graduates, 
she's going to become two people.

7
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:22,020
But until the two of them turn human, 
they can't both exist at the same time.

8
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:26,050
I get it. That's what you mean.

9
00:00:26,510 --> 00:00:31,070
This is Isaki's only chance, 
so we should hold two graduations for her!

10
00:00:31,070 --> 00:00:33,190
The next full moon's four days from now!

11
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:37,730
That'll be the last chance 
for us to meet the other Isaki.

12
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,420
The school's real graduation ceremony 
isn't for another week.

13
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:47,050
Why don't we hold our own ceremony 
on the full moon in four days?

14
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:50,330
You're right. I think that's a great idea.

15
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:53,530
It almost reminds me of a wedding!

16
00:00:53,530 --> 00:00:56,730
The kind with two ceremonies! How lovely!

17
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:00,910
Mr. Rei, what kind of 
wedding would you prefer?

18
00:01:00,910 --> 00:01:03,810
W-We're talking 
about graduations right now!

19
00:01:03,810 --> 00:01:08,460
Let's get back on topic and think 
about what to do for Isaki's graduation!

20
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:11,690
While we're at it, why 
don't we make it a surprise?

21
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:15,440
I like it! I'm all for a good surprise!

22
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,700
She won't know what's coming to her!

23
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:19,290
That's that, then!

24
00:01:19,290 --> 00:01:22,660
Let's keep it a secret 
from her until then!

25
00:01:25,130 --> 00:01:26,870
Good morning.

26
00:01:26,870 --> 00:01:31,090
Huh? Everyone's here early today.

27
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:33,460
Mathematics

28
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:33,460
I'm studying for my entrance exams.

29
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:35,980
Bowledoodle's so cute!

30
00:01:38,190 --> 00:01:41,010
Mr. Rei! I love, love, love you!

31
00:03:14,170 --> 00:03:18,870
The Misanthrope and the Comet's Pilgrimage

32
00:03:14,170 --> 00:03:18,870
The Misanthrope and the Comet's Pilgrimage

33
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:18,870
Episode 10

34
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:18,870
Episode 10

35
00:03:14,930 --> 00:03:17,700
A surprise graduation ceremony, huh?

36
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:20,840
If it's in the classroom, 
she might find out while we set up.

37
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:23,910
That's the biggest issue here.

38
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:27,180
We need to find somewhere 
that Isaki wouldn't go.

39
00:03:27,610 --> 00:03:30,360
How about the empty 
classroom next to the library?

40
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:34,030
She might find out 
when she goes to the library.

41
00:03:34,470 --> 00:03:36,310
What about the conference room?

42
00:03:36,310 --> 00:03:38,370
It's too close to the teachers' office.

43
00:03:38,370 --> 00:03:41,890
We can't be too rowdy 
with the other teachers nearby.

44
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:46,250
Where should it be, then?

45
00:03:46,250 --> 00:03:48,500
How about the A/V room?

46
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:50,130
Good idea!

47
00:03:50,130 --> 00:03:52,500
It's soundproof, and we 
can use the projector!

48
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,010
Sounds good to me!

49
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:56,400
I think so, too.

50
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,620
Yeah, sounds like our best choice.

51
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:00,050
What do you think?

52
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:02,180
I like the idea, too.

53
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:06,250
I'll find out if we can use 
the A/V room that day.

54
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:08,150
Thanks, Mr. Hitoma!

55
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:12,760
What kinda ceremony will it be for Ichaki?

56
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:16,310
I propose that we make it a fun one!

57
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:19,940
A serious ceremony will emphasize 
what a big milestone it is.

58
00:04:20,390 --> 00:04:22,920
They both have their charms, don't they?

59
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:27,460
<i>I like the do-it-yourself feel this has.</i>

60
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:32,470
<i>I'll have to do all I can to make it 
a good graduation ceremony.</i>

61
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:37,340
Advanced Class

62
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:37,380
Um...

63
00:04:38,090 --> 00:04:41,890
I feel like everyone's been 
acting distant to me lately.

64
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:43,180
What?

65
00:04:43,910 --> 00:04:47,140
Not to mention they all run 
off somewhere after school.

66
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:50,900
I-I don't think that's true.

67
00:04:51,130 --> 00:04:55,430
I don't have much time left 
to spend with them.

68
00:04:56,130 --> 00:04:59,770
But now they're all treating me 
differently than before.

69
00:05:00,650 --> 00:05:04,870
I can't help but feel 
like they're avoiding me...

70
00:05:07,020 --> 00:05:12,100
Ohgami, do you mind if I share 
how you feel with the others?

71
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:12,850
What?

72
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:14,940
Well...

73
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:20,180
If they really <i>are</i> avoiding me, 
I don't think I could ever recover.

74
00:05:20,470 --> 00:05:22,430
I can guarantee that's not the case.

75
00:05:22,850 --> 00:05:23,640
Still...

76
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:25,420
Don't worry!

77
00:05:26,030 --> 00:05:27,890
That's definitely not what's going on!

78
00:05:28,290 --> 00:05:30,950
R-Really?

79
00:05:30,950 --> 00:05:32,550
Yeah! Yep! Uh-huh!

80
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:34,770
If you say so...

81
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:36,810
Then sure, go ahead.

82
00:05:36,810 --> 00:05:38,490
Thanks, Ohgami!

83
00:05:38,970 --> 00:05:40,860
You just wait right here!

84
00:05:48,990 --> 00:05:51,540
A-Are you all right, Mr. Hitoma?!

85
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:55,000
Di... Di... Di...

86
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,710
Die?! Please don't die on me!

87
00:05:57,710 --> 00:06:01,590
N-No... Directly to the A/V room...

88
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:02,740
Huh?

89
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:05,470
A/V Room

90
00:06:08,090 --> 00:06:09,780
Can I go inside?

91
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:11,000
Yeah.

92
00:06:11,390 --> 00:06:12,850
Here I go...

93
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:15,440
Excuse me...

94
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:17,900
Congratulations on graduating!

95
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:21,640
We're sorry we made you worry!

96
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:23,880
U-Um...

97
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:25,540
We're sorry.

98
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:27,950
You know how tomorrow's the full moon?

99
00:06:28,330 --> 00:06:33,540
So we were planning on holding 
a graduation ceremony for the other Isaki.

100
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:40,300
It was meant to be a surprise, 
but not if it ends up worrying you. Isaki.

101
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:42,930
We want to congratulate both Isakis!

102
00:06:43,250 --> 00:06:44,050
What?

103
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:48,350
Wow, it looks amazing!

104
00:06:49,270 --> 00:06:52,170
You prepared all of this?

105
00:06:52,170 --> 00:06:54,720
That's right!

106
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:57,070
We did our best to make it look cute!

107
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:58,780
It's fine, I guess.

108
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:03,550
Usami says that, 
but she got pretty into it, too.

109
00:07:03,550 --> 00:07:06,280
She was like, "I hope Isaki likes it!"

110
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,630
You don't need to tell her that!

111
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:11,700
Everyone... I'm so glad...

112
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:16,500
I was worried that you 
were all avoiding me...

113
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:21,900
Everyone here is happy for you, Ohgami.

114
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:25,280
Yes! Thank you so much!

115
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:29,250
Well, all we're doing is having 
the graduation ceremony tomorrow.

116
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,210
That may be so...

117
00:07:31,210 --> 00:07:36,480
but I also thought it'd be nice 
to let Isaki celebrate her graduation.

118
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:41,940
So I'm happy to see that
you all care so much about Isaki.

119
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:44,650
Don't get the wrong idea.

120
00:07:45,950 --> 00:07:48,110
It's not just for Isaki tomorrow.

121
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:50,470
We care about the Isaki here, too.

122
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:51,860
That's right!

123
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:54,150
Don't forget about that!

124
00:07:54,660 --> 00:07:58,610
To tell you the truth, 
I was jealous of you and Isaki.

125
00:07:59,110 --> 00:08:04,550
You both value and care 
equally as much for each other.

126
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:09,050
I hope the two of you find 
wonderful things in your futures!

127
00:08:09,770 --> 00:08:13,420
Everyone... Thank you so much!

128
00:08:14,350 --> 00:08:17,180
Happy Graduation Isaki

129
00:08:14,350 --> 00:08:17,180
The Next Day

130
00:08:21,870 --> 00:08:23,860
We will hereby award the diploma.

131
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:27,030
Diploma of Graduation
Isaki Ohgami
This certifies that the above individual has completed all of the prescribed studies.
 Shiranui Private High School
Principal Shiro Karasuma

132
00:08:24,330 --> 00:08:27,070
Graduating student, Isaki Ohgami.

133
00:08:27,070 --> 00:08:28,450
Yes!

134
00:08:32,940 --> 00:08:35,700
Isaki. Congratulations on graduating.

135
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:38,420
Thanks, Tobari.

136
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:43,130
I know that you'll do just fine 
in the human world, Isaki.

137
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:44,690
You have my word.

138
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:48,880
I hope you lead a wonderful life 
without any regrets.

139
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:49,780
Yeah!

140
00:08:50,350 --> 00:08:54,970
Let's go grab some tasty desserts someday 
when we're both human!

141
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:58,310
Yeah! One day for sure!

142
00:09:04,910 --> 00:09:07,110
Thanks, everyone!

143
00:09:10,030 --> 00:09:14,070
3 Days Later

144
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:14,550
We will hereby award the diploma.

145
00:09:15,650 --> 00:09:18,030
Graduating student, Isaki Ohgami.

146
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:20,450
Y-Yes!

147
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:27,050
Isaki Ohgami.

148
00:09:27,050 --> 00:09:29,630
Congratulations to you!

149
00:09:30,110 --> 00:09:31,710
Principal!

150
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:37,480
Your graduation is the culmination 
of your hard-earned efforts.

151
00:09:37,820 --> 00:09:40,310
Nothing can change that fact.

152
00:09:40,310 --> 00:09:46,380
I'll always remember 
with pride having had you as a student.

153
00:09:57,910 --> 00:10:02,680
I'm so sad that Ichaki's graduating!

154
00:10:01,650 --> 00:10:03,580
Shut up, Machi!

155
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:07,460
I can't help it!

156
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:11,130
P-Please don't cry, Machi...

157
00:10:12,470 --> 00:10:15,010
Now <i>you're</i> crying, Isaki!

158
00:10:15,010 --> 00:10:17,930
Hey now, lay off her for today.

159
00:10:17,930 --> 00:10:21,770
That's right. Aren't you sad, too, Sui?

160
00:10:21,770 --> 00:10:22,660
Huh?!

161
00:10:23,010 --> 00:10:24,170
Well...

162
00:10:24,170 --> 00:10:26,440
It'll feel like something's missing.

163
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:28,170
Usami...

164
00:10:28,170 --> 00:10:32,940
I'll be sad to miss out 
on that surly affection of yours.

165
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:34,160
<i>That's</i> why?!

166
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:39,240
Mr. Hitoma!

167
00:10:39,830 --> 00:10:41,210
Mr. Hitoma.

168
00:10:42,660 --> 00:10:45,640
Thank you for everything 
over the past two years.

169
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:48,020
Y-Yeah.

170
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:54,940
The Isaki within me has served 
as a beacon of hope all this time.

171
00:10:56,090 --> 00:11:01,770
You gave us the chance for Isaki 
and I to come to an understanding.

172
00:11:01,990 --> 00:11:04,870
I can't thank you enough.

173
00:11:05,190 --> 00:11:06,410
Ohgami...

174
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:09,220
I should be thanking you.

175
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:15,180
Ohgami, your actions and outcomes came 
from your own decisions.

176
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:18,610
I know that you two will do just fine.

177
00:11:20,100 --> 00:11:24,920
I wish the two of you 
happy lives going forward.

178
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:26,980
Mr. Hitoma.

179
00:11:27,590 --> 00:11:29,190
Thank you very much!

180
00:11:29,630 --> 00:11:31,960
My wish is the same!

181
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,090
Me, too!

182
00:11:34,620 --> 00:11:37,050
Thank you all so much!

183
00:11:38,210 --> 00:11:39,650
Congratulations once again!

184
00:11:39,650 --> 00:11:41,010
Congrats!

185
00:11:40,930 --> 00:11:43,430
Conference Room

186
00:11:42,390 --> 00:11:43,490
Here we go!

187
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:45,960
Cheers, everyone!

188
00:11:46,310 --> 00:11:49,150
Cheers!

189
00:11:50,530 --> 00:11:52,140
Oh, human.

190
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:55,460
Not drinking much, are we?

191
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:59,500
C'mon, let me top you off.

192
00:12:00,170 --> 00:12:01,890
Oh, thank you.

193
00:12:01,890 --> 00:12:04,760
Wait, what are <i>you</i> 
doing here, Miss Alice?!

194
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:08,540
Figured I'd celebrate 
the occasion by sneaking in.

195
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:10,040
It looked like fun.

196
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:12,190
Is that really okay?

197
00:12:12,190 --> 00:12:14,090
Yeah, it's fine.

198
00:12:14,090 --> 00:12:19,170
I've cast a spell on myself so I can
only be seen by people I've met before.

199
00:12:19,170 --> 00:12:21,140
Mr. Hitoma, who's this?

200
00:12:21,580 --> 00:12:22,260
Huh?

201
00:12:22,570 --> 00:12:24,190
<i>He can see you just fine!</i>

202
00:12:24,850 --> 00:12:26,800
Hey, you're...

203
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:27,860
Miss Alice.

204
00:12:27,860 --> 00:12:30,840
You shouldn't get 
in a married man's face like that.

205
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:33,220
Huh? He's taken?

206
00:12:33,810 --> 00:12:36,470
Mr. Hitoma, who <i>is</i> this?

207
00:12:36,470 --> 00:12:39,860
Alice! How dare you show your face here!

208
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:41,000
Ugh, rats.

209
00:12:43,470 --> 00:12:47,660
Oh, is she an acquaintance 
of the principal?

210
00:12:48,010 --> 00:12:50,850
Um... You could say that.

211
00:12:51,290 --> 00:12:53,020
What's up?

212
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:57,070
It seems a friend 
of the principal joined our party.

213
00:12:57,340 --> 00:12:59,250
Never mind that, Satoru.

214
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:02,140
Yuki's already on her 
sixth bottle, you know.

215
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:03,240
What?!

216
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:10,250
Gotta start with the most expensive 
and delicious booze first...

217
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:13,970
Mr. Hoshino's got it rough...

218
00:13:19,850 --> 00:13:21,550
I feel awful...

219
00:13:22,250 --> 00:13:23,850
Get to work.

220
00:13:23,850 --> 00:13:24,790
What?

221
00:13:24,790 --> 00:13:26,630
Why are you slacking off?

222
00:13:26,630 --> 00:13:29,800
I had too much to drink, 
and now I'm hungover.

223
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:34,770
I'm getting second thoughts 
about giving you this important job.

224
00:13:35,490 --> 00:13:36,730
A job?

225
00:13:36,730 --> 00:13:40,610
Hitoma. I want you to be my mailman.

226
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,400
Excuse me?

227
00:13:44,710 --> 00:13:46,820
I wrote this letter while 
I was doing my assignment.

228
00:13:47,290 --> 00:13:50,520
I want you to deliver it 
to Seiko in my place.

229
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:57,130
I would have liked to go myself, 
but I didn't manage to graduate.

230
00:13:57,790 --> 00:14:00,840
That's why I'm here to ask you, Hitoma.

231
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:02,120
Usami.

232
00:14:04,250 --> 00:14:06,260
I want you to visit her grave.

233
00:14:06,990 --> 00:14:11,720
School rules forbid any unauthorized 
transmission of information off-campus.

234
00:14:12,050 --> 00:14:13,450
I know that!

235
00:14:14,030 --> 00:14:16,490
I figured it'd be a long shot.

236
00:14:16,490 --> 00:14:17,530
I see.

237
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:22,120
Is it okay if I take this letter for now?

238
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:24,580
I'll see what the principal has to say.

239
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:28,010
Hitoma. Thanks.

240
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:31,710
I can't promise I'll deliver it to Seiko.

241
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:33,310
That's okay.

242
00:14:33,850 --> 00:14:36,150
If you can't, then I'll accept it.

243
00:14:37,150 --> 00:14:38,940
I have no other choice.

244
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:42,350
Okay. I'll try asking.

245
00:14:51,470 --> 00:14:54,290
<i>I take the bus from here?</i>

246
00:14:54,930 --> 00:14:56,870
<i>The bus stop should be...</i>

247
00:14:56,870 --> 00:14:58,470
Oh, excuse me.

248
00:15:01,340 --> 00:15:03,150
Could I ask you something?

249
00:15:05,130 --> 00:15:06,310
I'm sorry.

250
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:09,110
I assumed you were a local.

251
00:15:09,430 --> 00:15:13,020
No, we just happened to have the same
destination, and I know the way there.

252
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:17,620
My student asked me to deliver a letter 
to the grave of her former caretaker.

253
00:15:18,010 --> 00:15:21,120
Oh, what a wonderful teacher you are.

254
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:23,640
No, I wouldn't go that far.

255
00:15:24,570 --> 00:15:28,260
I'm sure she would have 
wanted to make the trip herself.

256
00:15:28,710 --> 00:15:31,240
A letter for her caretaker's grave?

257
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,030
What an admirable girl.

258
00:15:33,030 --> 00:15:34,760
Yes. Oh...

259
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:38,540
I forgot to introduce myself, 
but my name is Rei Hitoma.

260
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:40,770
How polite of you.

261
00:15:41,100 --> 00:15:45,320
As for me, I'm Sae Kizaki.

262
00:15:45,630 --> 00:15:47,010
Ms. Kizaki?

263
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:48,490
What?

264
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:53,810
Um, would your mother's name 
happen to be Seiko Kizaki?

265
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:55,020
What?

266
00:15:55,640 --> 00:15:56,980
How do you know that?

267
00:16:01,110 --> 00:16:04,150
Kizaki Family

268
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:15,080
Thank you for waiting. Go ahead.

269
00:16:15,930 --> 00:16:17,080
Pardon my intrusion.

270
00:16:18,390 --> 00:16:20,280
<i>Mrs. Seiko, it's nice to meet you.</i>

271
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:23,380
<i>I'm Rei Hitoma, Usami's homeroom teacher.</i>

272
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:32,060
<i>Usami studies and works hard every day 
with the help of her classmates.</i>

273
00:16:32,970 --> 00:16:38,910
<i>As her teacher, I know she's diligent,
and cares very much for those around her.</i>

274
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:42,710
<i>I've come here today 
with a letter from Usami.</i>

275
00:16:44,530 --> 00:16:47,640
<i>I also received a letter 
from her the other day.</i>

276
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:51,090
<i>It was a wonderful, honest, 
and heartfelt letter.</i>

277
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:57,900
<i>I'm sure she's put great thought 
into writing a wonderful letter for you.</i>

278
00:17:00,090 --> 00:17:01,700
<i>I'm here in her place today,</i>

279
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:04,610
<i>but I know that she'll graduate 
and visit in person one day.</i>

280
00:17:05,470 --> 00:17:07,870
<i>Please wait until that day comes.</i>

281
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:11,320
<i>That's all from me.</i>

282
00:17:14,510 --> 00:17:16,520
Ms. Sae, thank you 
for letting me pay a visit.

283
00:17:16,950 --> 00:17:20,190
Not at all. I'm sure 
my mother's delighted.

284
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:23,570
Cosmos...

285
00:17:24,650 --> 00:17:28,870
Your student must have 
known my mother very well.

286
00:17:28,870 --> 00:17:29,800
What?

287
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:33,390
Cosmos were my mother's favorite flowers.

288
00:17:33,930 --> 00:17:39,270
Their color reminded her of a stuffed 
rabbit she had ever since she was a child.

289
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:44,280
But it had gone missing.

290
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:48,330
I looked for it before the funeral, 
but I never found it.

291
00:17:49,090 --> 00:17:53,660
I still regret not being 
able to place it in her coffin.

292
00:17:57,010 --> 00:17:58,990
Thank you for everything today.

293
00:17:58,990 --> 00:18:02,040
Oh, thank you as well.

294
00:18:02,570 --> 00:18:04,900
Please give my regards to your student.

295
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:05,960
Will do.

296
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:08,680
So long.

297
00:18:11,510 --> 00:18:12,420
Excuse me!

298
00:18:14,310 --> 00:18:15,640
The stuffed rabbit!

299
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:20,410
Actually, my student got it 
as a gift from Mrs. Kizaki.

300
00:18:20,410 --> 00:18:21,220
What?

301
00:18:21,580 --> 00:18:22,650
It was fall two years ago.

302
00:18:22,650 --> 00:18:25,090
My student visited her in the hospital, 
and received it then.

303
00:18:25,870 --> 00:18:27,550
So there's no need to worry!

304
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:31,410
Her stuffed rabbit is alive 
and well to this very day!

305
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:33,420
Are you serious?

306
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:36,320
Yes! Usami's doing just fine!

307
00:18:40,210 --> 00:18:41,450
What a relief.

308
00:18:43,150 --> 00:18:48,760
Usami loves gossip, 
so make sure she talks a lot to her.

309
00:18:49,210 --> 00:18:51,550
Yes, I'll let her know.

310
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:54,800
Here's my contact information.

311
00:18:56,030 --> 00:18:57,910
Please give this to your student.

312
00:18:58,580 --> 00:19:00,730
She can reach out if she ever needs help.

313
00:19:02,170 --> 00:19:05,940
Even if she doesn't, 
I'd love to speak with her someday.

314
00:19:06,230 --> 00:19:07,830
Yes, I'll make it happen.

315
00:19:17,630 --> 00:19:18,740
Usami?

316
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:21,990
Did you deliver my letter to Seiko?

317
00:19:22,390 --> 00:19:23,300
Yeah.

318
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:26,630
And as luck would have it, 
I also ran into her daughter, Sae.

319
00:19:26,630 --> 00:19:28,220
You got to meet Sae?!

320
00:19:28,650 --> 00:19:31,130
Was she still a cheeky brat?

321
00:19:31,450 --> 00:19:34,910
What exactly is your image of Ms. Sae?

322
00:19:35,570 --> 00:19:37,800
A rotten brat who never listens.

323
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:39,340
What'd you two talk about?

324
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:44,790
She told me that Usami loves gossip, 
so you should talk a lot to her.

325
00:19:44,790 --> 00:19:48,090
Sae and Seiko are 
the ones who love to gossip.

326
00:19:48,780 --> 00:19:51,730
Also, I received Ms. Sae's 
contact information.

327
00:19:53,890 --> 00:19:56,400
Once you graduate, you can go meet her.

328
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:58,660
Yeah! Got it!

329
00:19:58,660 --> 00:20:00,490
I'll try even harder!

330
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:04,410
I'll graduate, and see 
how big Sae's gotten!

331
00:20:04,770 --> 00:20:05,780
That's right.

332
00:20:06,470 --> 00:20:08,900
Now I have another new goal!

333
00:20:09,650 --> 00:20:10,630
Hitoma!

334
00:20:10,630 --> 00:20:13,300
Thanks for going to talk with Sae!

335
00:20:13,750 --> 00:20:17,990
I'd love to talk to Sae, too, someday!

336
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:20,780
Director's Office

337
00:20:20,270 --> 00:20:23,170
Okay, let's begin our interview.

338
00:20:23,170 --> 00:20:25,100
How was the past year for you?

339
00:20:26,090 --> 00:20:29,410
I learned even more over the last year.

340
00:20:30,370 --> 00:20:32,330
Weakness can be just as necessary a trait.

341
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:35,570
The people around you 
will be there to help.

342
00:20:36,230 --> 00:20:38,770
That shooting stars 
in the summer are beautiful.

343
00:20:39,370 --> 00:20:41,050
How important it is to think for yourself.

344
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:47,480
And that you should say what's 
on your mind when you can.

345
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:51,750
I see. One last question.

346
00:20:52,250 --> 00:20:55,370
Hey, Mr. Hitoma. Do you like humans?

347
00:20:57,220 --> 00:20:59,120
I hate humans.

348
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:03,290
That said, I think there's more 
about them I can forgive since last year.

349
00:21:03,820 --> 00:21:06,630
I see. That's just like you.

350
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:10,770
Will there be any intermediate 
students moving up this year?

351
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:12,430
There sure are.

352
00:21:12,430 --> 00:21:15,210
And we're getting a new teacher.

353
00:21:15,210 --> 00:21:16,270
Seriously?!

354
00:21:16,270 --> 00:21:17,190
Seriously.

355
00:21:17,190 --> 00:21:19,630
I wonder what they're like...

356
00:21:19,630 --> 00:21:21,110
Want to see the file?

357
00:21:21,110 --> 00:21:22,450
Can I really?!

358
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:24,550
You're all ears, huh?

359
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:30,060
You might want to take a moment 
to prepare yourself, Mr. Hitoma.

360
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:34,470
This teacher will be the assistant 
homeroom teacher for the advanced class.

361
00:21:35,130 --> 00:21:38,800
So you mean I'll be 
working with them a lot?

362
00:21:39,210 --> 00:21:40,620
That's right.

363
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:42,220
Are you ready?

364
00:21:42,890 --> 00:21:43,580
Yeah.

365
00:21:44,130 --> 00:21:45,850
Take a look, then.

366
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:51,080
Resume

367
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:51,080
Furigana       Mirai Haruna

368
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:51,080
Full Name      Mirai Haruna

369
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:57,330
Mirai Haruna.

370
00:21:58,050 --> 00:22:00,510
She'll be your junior co-worker 
starting with the new term.

371
00:23:32,950 --> 00:23:40,020
Next Episode:

372
00:23:32,950 --> 00:23:40,020
The Misanthrope and the Nigh Past

